  "content": {
    "id": "p24-q1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "Use graphing software to sketch various functions in the form\n$$f(x)=|ax+b|\\pm|cx+d|,$$\nfor varying values of $a$, $b$, $c$ and $d$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p24-q1-root-run-1",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "",
        "prompt": "",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p24-q1-a",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "a",
            "prompt": "How many different general ‘shapes’ can you observe forming?",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "Answers vary according to how general shapes are grouped.",
              "worked": "Compare graphs with coincident and distinct turning points, equal and unequal coefficient magnitudes, and both choices of sign. Reflected versions may be counted separately or grouped together, so the question does not determine a unique number.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 10
          },
          {
            "id": "p24-q1-b",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "b",
            "prompt": "List all the possible general shapes that you find, and state the particular values of $a$, $b$, $c$ and $d$ that resulted in each one.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "Examples: V, $|x|+|x|$; V with an extra corner on one arm, $|2x|+|x-1|$; flat-bottomed V, $|x+1|+|x-2|$; inverted V, $|x|-|2x|$; inverted V with an extra corner, $|x|-|2x-2|$; ramp between horizontal rays, $|x|-|x-1|$; horizontal line, $|x|-|x|$. Reflections give further orientations.",
              "worked": "One possible collection is shown below. The parameter order is $(a,b,c,d)$.\n\nV: choose the plus sign and $(1,0,1,0)$.\n$$f(x)=2|x|.$$\n\nV with an extra corner on one arm: choose the plus sign and $(2,0,1,-1)$.\n$$f(x)=\\begin{cases}-3x+1,&x<0,\\\\x+1,&0\\le x\\le1,\\\\3x-1,&x>1.\\end{cases}$$\n\nFlat-bottomed V: choose the plus sign and $(1,1,1,-2)$.\n$$f(x)=\\begin{cases}-2x+1,&x<-1,\\\\3,&-1\\le x\\le2,\\\\2x-1,&x>2.\\end{cases}$$\n\nInverted V: choose the minus sign and $(1,0,2,0)$.\n$$f(x)=-|x|.$$\n\nInverted V with an extra corner: choose the minus sign and $(1,0,2,-2)$.\n$$f(x)=\\begin{cases}x-2,&x<0,\\\\3x-2,&0\\le x\\le1,\\\\-x+2,&x>1.\\end{cases}$$\n\nRamp between horizontal rays: choose the minus sign and $(1,0,1,-1)$.\n$$f(x)=\\begin{cases}-1,&x<0,\\\\2x-1,&0\\le x\\le1,\\\\1,&x>1.\\end{cases}$$\n\nHorizontal line: choose the minus sign and $(1,0,1,0)$.\n$$f(x)=0.$$\n\nReplacing $x$ by $-x$ gives the reflected orientations. These examples illustrate shape families; the source does not define a unique rule for counting them.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 69
          },
          {
            "id": "p24-q1-c",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "c",
            "prompt": "For $a\\ne0$ and $c\\ne0$, what is the significance of $x=-\\dfrac{b}{a}$ and $x=-\\dfrac{d}{c}$?",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "They are the zeros of the two absolute-value arguments and the possible locations of corners in the combined graph.",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}ax+b&=0\\\\x&=-\\frac{b}{a}\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}cx+d&=0\\\\x&=-\\frac{d}{c}\\end{align*}$$\nEach argument changes sign at its zero. These values divide the domain into regions where the absolute-value signs can be removed consistently. Coincident changes can cancel in a difference, so a visible corner need not remain.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 18
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q2-root",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "",
        "prompt": "Consider the equation\n$$f(x)=|x+1|+|x-2|.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p24-q2-a",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "d",
            "prompt": "From your findings in Question 1, what kind of shape should the graph have?",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "A flat-bottomed V.",
              "worked": "The two absolute-value terms have equal coefficient magnitudes and different zeros. Between their zeros, one term increases at the same rate as the other decreases, giving a horizontal middle section.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 10
          },
          {
            "id": "p24-q2-b",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "e",
            "prompt": {
              "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
              "version": 1,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p24-q2-b-prompt",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "fontSize": null,
                  "align": "left",
                  "spaceBefore": 0,
                  "spaceAfter": 2,
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "indent": 0,
                  "inlines": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "What are the ‘critical’ ",
                      "marks": []
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "math",
                      "latex": "x",
                      "display": false
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "-coordinates where the shape may change?",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$x=-1$ and $x=2$.",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x+1&=0\\\\x&=-1\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}x-2&=0\\\\x&=2\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 0
          },
          {
            "id": "p24-q2-c",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "f",
            "prompt": "These critical points split the $x$-axis into three regions. Write down what the three regions are as inequalities.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$x<-1$, $-1\\le x\\le2$, $x>2$.",
              "worked": "Using the endpoint convention in part (e), the regions are\n$$x<-1,\\qquad-1\\le x\\le2,\\qquad x>2.$$\nBoth adjoining expressions agree at each boundary.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 10
          },
