            "answer": {
              "short": "$f(x)=\\begin{cases}2x-1,&x>2,\\\\3,&-1\\le x\\le2,\\\\-2x+1,&x<-1.\\end{cases}$",
              "worked": "For $x>2$, both arguments are positive:\n$$\\begin{align*}f(x)&=(x+1)+(x-2)\\\\f(x)&=2x-1.\\end{align*}$$\nFor $-1\\le x\\le2$, $x+1\\ge0$ and $x-2\\le0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}f(x)&=(x+1)+(-x+2)\\\\f(x)&=3.\\end{align*}$$\nFor $x<-1$, both arguments are negative:\n$$\\begin{align*}f(x)&=(-x-1)+(-x+2)\\\\f(x)&=-2x+1.\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
